  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>A) Phenol reacts with chloroform in presence of aqueous sodium hydroxide to form salicylaldehyde, which is named as&nbsp;Riemer-Tiemann reaction.</p><p>B)Phenol when heated with zinc dust forms benzene.</p><p>C)Oxidation of phenol with acidified potassium dichromate gives benzoquinone.</p><p>D)&nbsp;Bromination of phenol in presence of&nbsp;a&nbsp;non-polar solvent like CS<sub>2</sub>&nbsp;gives para-bromo phenol as the major product.</p><p>(A)&nbsp;<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/a0edd389-34cb-4c72-8e97-b0f37e84995f-image.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 106px;\" /></p><p>(B)</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/8fe870d5-fe9a-4dd0-b05e-a28cb446422e-image.png\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 126px;\" /></p><p>(C)&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/8479b330-1dc5-4277-8eb8-4c49564637a8-image.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 131px;\" /></p><p>(D)</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/a9fbbac5-f2b9-4ce4-a9f4-5de89edd21e4-image.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 141px;\" /></p>",
